{%- comment -%}
Paste this into the plugin's Shared markup box. TRMNL prepends it to every
view before rendering, so each layout can `{% render "chart", series: series %}`
and `{% render "freshness", fetched_at: fetched_at, age_seconds: age_seconds %}`.
The bars use the framework's flex and size classes; only each bar's height is
inline, because it comes from the data. Placed directly in a `layout--col`,
`stretch-y` gives the chart whatever height the numbers leave, on every
screen size TRMNL renders for.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% template chart %}
<div class="flex flex--row flex--bottom gap--xsmall w--full stretch-y">
  {%- assign ceiling = series | map: "views" | sort | last -%}
  {%- if ceiling == 0 -%}{%- assign ceiling = 1 -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- for point in series -%}
  {%- assign height = point.views | times: 100 | divided_by: ceiling -%}
  {%- comment -%}
  Integer division floors, so a real but small day would round to 0% and
  vanish. A day that happened always draws something.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if height == 0 and point.views > 0 -%}{%- assign height = 1 -%}{%- endif -%}
  <div class="grow bg--black" style="height:{{ height }}%"></div>
  {%- endfor -%}
</div>
{% endtemplate %}
{% template freshness %}
{%- comment -%}
TRMNL keeps showing the last screen it drew, so the fetch time is always on
it. 7200 seconds is the PNG renderer's AGED_AFTER_SECONDS. Red reaches only
colour screens; the bit-depth classes keep the warning solid black on grey
and black-and-white ones, where red would dither.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if age_seconds > 7200 -%}
<span class="instance text--red 1bit:text--black 2bit:text--black 4bit:text--black">Refresh delayed · {{ fetched_at | slice: 0, 10 }} {{ fetched_at | slice: 11, 5 }} UTC</span>
{%- else -%}
<span class="instance">Updated {{ fetched_at | slice: 0, 10 }} {{ fetched_at | slice: 11, 5 }} UTC</span>
{%- endif -%}
{% endtemplate %}
